// APW-6 -- Window-boundary burst (CORRECT): "at most 3 events per day".
//
// The *intent* is a per-window cap.  The *fix* is a sliding window (no hard
// reset at the boundary), so the total admitted across windows stays bounded
// by the cap -- no 2x burst across the reset.
//
// This is a *forward-looking* sample: Dogwood's roadmap lists absolute-time
// windows, but they are not in the language yet, so this does not lower to a
// ROTN shape.  The hand-written oracle (rot.shapes.build_window_boundary_ir)
// models the sliding window and is what ROTN decides: PROVEN.
//
// See: docs/apw-catalog.md (APW-6), tests/test_apw6.py.

@id("apw6_correct")
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Send",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (sum 1 for (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 1d (Drupe::Action::"Send"::request{} && tp(t))
    )) > 3
};
